Key: α∈F shifty ⇔ its polynomial A(x)=∑α(i)x^i (deg≤8, coeff∈ℤ) divides x^c(1+x^m) for some c,m. Hence A(x)=±x^c·D(x) where D is product of cyclotomic Φ_n with n even, all having same v₂(n)=a, and Σφ(n)≤8.  

List even n with φ≤8:  
a=1: n={2(φ1),6(2),10(4),14(6),18(6),30(8)}  
a=2: n={4(2),12(4),20(8)}  
a=3: n={8(4),24(8)}  
a=4: n={16(8)}  

For each a, take any non‑empty subset S with total degree d=Σφ(n)≤8. Each yields (8−d+1) shifts c and 2 signs ⇒ contribution 2(8−d+1). Add empty set once (monomials): 2·9=18.  

Summing over all subsets gives 160 shifty functions.  

Pitfalls: avoid double‑counting empty set across a; ensure all n share same v₂; only consider φ≤8.
